From aac85bf69f6b1b69b3c120079057da0a0dcb097e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 05:41:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/51] Fix choosing a new cover image in the cover manager

Two things the page relies on in Chromium fail in WebKit:
- Re-upload clicks a file input that is never added to the document;
  WebKit may collect it while the open panel is up, so the chosen file
  never arrives. Keep such inputs in the document until the choice.
- Its image loader appends ?<timestamp> to blob: URLs, which WebKit
  cannot load, so the editor kept the previous picture and Confirm
  uploaded the old cover again. Drop the query from blob: URLs.

Adds test hooks for hosted pages (script evaluation, real clicks, a
preset file for the chooser via LIVEHIME_E2E_PICK_FILE) and an E2E check
that replaced the room cover with a chosen local image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
